        "blast_url": "https://blast.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/Blast.cgi?PAGE_TYPE=BlastSearch&PROG_DEF=blastn&BLAST_SPEC=GDH_GCA_988240805.1",
        "comments": "The assembly of 'Hoplostethus mediterraneus' (fHopMed1) is based on 28X ONT data and 171X Arima Hi-C data generated as part of the ATLASea programme (https://www.atlasea.fr). The assembly process included the following steps: initial ONT assembly generation with Flye, removal of contaminant sequences using Context, removal of haplotypic duplications using purge_dups, and Hi-C-based scaffolding with YaHS. In total, 7 contigs were identified as contaminants (bacterial, archaeal, or viral), totaling 0.128 Mb (with the largest being 0.034 Mb). Additionally, 397 regions totaling 9.504 Mb (with the largest being 0.136 Mb) were identified as haplotypic duplications and removed. Mitochondrial genome was assembled using ptGAUL. Finally, the primary assembly was analyzed and manually improved using Pretext. During manual curation, 20 haplotypic regions were removed, totaling 0.61Mb (with the largest being 0.11Mb). Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by Hi-C data were named in order of size.",
